# Only needed for optional local image OCR. No cloud or account credentials.
# Point to an already installed, trusted Tesseract executable.
BILLFIT_TESSERACT_PATH=
# This example is documentation; BillFit does not automatically load .env files.
# Set the variable in the CLI/host environment. It is never a model-supplied argument.
# Parser limits are internal: 25 MB file, 25 PDF/image pages, 30 seconds per
# parser invocation, 2 MB combined OCR output / 8 MB combined PDF worker output.
# Child stderr is discarded; returned fields/snippets still reach the calling host.
# Low/unknown OCR confidence and all candidate values need visual user review.
# The optional --sdk server admits two bill extractions per server instance.
# BILL_PARSER_BUSY rejects excess work without queueing or automatic retry.
# SDK cancellation cleans up owned parsing; the synchronous legacy shim does not.
# This is not a global process limit or a hard memory sandbox.
# Optional image preparation: install requirements-image-input.txt in the server
# environment, then explicitly supply ocr_rotation_degrees and/or ocr_deskew.
# No new environment variable enables it. It accepts one image page, up to
# 25 million pixels / 20,000 pixels per side and 25 MB for source and derived PNG.
# Its child has a 10-second cap within the shared 30-second preparation/OCR budget.
# Evidence coordinates refer to original encoded pixels, before EXIF display rotation.
